<Page
  title="About SnarkBrain"
  description="SnarkBrain is an independent archive of fact-checks about claims circulating online about Ethan Klein, Hila Klein and the H3 Podcast."
  schemaType="AboutPage"
>
  <p>
    Accusations about Ethan and Hila Klein spread fast, usually as a cropped clip, a screenshot or a secondhand summary.
    The original context almost always exists, but it's buried in hours of footage, court dockets and old posts.
    SnarkBrain gathers that context in one place so anyone can check a claim against the evidence for themselves.
  </p>
  <p>
    For years, Ethan and Hila Klein and their businesses have been targets of harassment from a dedicated online
    community whose members call themselves “snarkers.” Its narratives have distorted the couple's public image and
    caused irreparable damage to their reputation. SnarkBrain is an attempt to clarify things, while staying honest
    about the facts, even when they're unflattering.
  </p>

  <h2>The name</h2>
  <p>
    The term describes the mindset these fact-checks respond to: treating every clip in the worst possible light, and
    repeating a claim because it fits, not because it's true.
  </p>

  <h2>Who writes it</h2>
  <p>
    SnarkBrain is written by members of the H3 community, and we don't pretend otherwise. That's exactly why every
    factual statement on this site links to a source you can check. You shouldn't have to take our word for anything.
  </p>
  <p>
    Contributors include
    <a href="https://linktr.ee/FoopaTroopaH3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Foopa Troopa
    </a>{" "}
    and
    <a href="https://www.reddit.com/user/GrapeTickler/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Grape Tickler
    </a>
    , along with anonymous community members.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>SnarkBrain is not affiliated with or endorsed by the H3 Podcast, Ethan Klein or Hila Klein.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    To report an error, share new evidence or suggest a claim to check, email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Read how we work in our <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
